00:33:32,580 --> 00:33:35,880
 And then March of 2020, the world shut down,

763
00:33:35,880 --> 00:33:38,420
 all camps shut down, there goes all the disposable

764
00:33:38,420 --> 00:33:40,680
 extra income, and then we had an intern

765
00:33:40,680 --> 00:33:42,900
 living with us that summer.

766
00:33:42,900 --> 00:33:45,820
 And I remember writing in my Bible,

767
00:33:45,820 --> 00:33:50,260
 in April of 2020, "God, we trust you."

768
00:33:50,260 --> 00:33:53,620
 Then crazy things started to happen.

769
00:33:54,740 --> 00:33:58,020
 In April of that year, our landlords were renting.

770
00:33:58,020 --> 00:34:00,840
 Our landlords, he calls me, he's like,

771
00:34:00,840 --> 00:34:03,440
 "Hey man, all this COVID stuff's crazy.

772
00:34:03,440 --> 00:34:06,380
 "Don't worry about paying rent in April."

773
00:34:06,380 --> 00:34:07,700
 Don't worry, what?

774
00:34:07,700 --> 00:34:09,380
 What land, I mean, has that ever happened

775
00:34:09,380 --> 00:34:11,100
 in the history of landlordness?

776
00:34:11,100 --> 00:34:13,220
 Like, that's crazy.

777
00:34:13,220 --> 00:34:15,700
 Wow, you know, hang up.

778
00:34:15,700 --> 00:34:17,780
 Then we get a letter in the mail

779
00:34:17,780 --> 00:34:21,500
 from a missionary we had supported, $100 a month.

780
00:34:21,500 --> 00:34:24,160
 We had just, we'd said, "We wanna sow into your ministry,

781
00:34:24,160 --> 00:34:25,220
 "we wanna support you."

782
00:34:25,220 --> 00:34:28,260
 They wrote us a check for $1,200 saying,

783
00:34:28,260 --> 00:34:29,620
 "We wanna give back to you everything

784
00:34:29,620 --> 00:34:30,820
 "you gave to us this year."

785
00:34:30,820 --> 00:34:32,900
 We just felt compelled to.

786
00:34:32,900 --> 00:34:35,460
 Just like, wow, and things like that just kept happening,

787
00:34:35,460 --> 00:34:37,940
 happening, happening, and my wife and I look back at that

788
00:34:37,940 --> 00:34:40,140
 and we just go, wow, even though we're in a different

789
00:34:40,140 --> 00:34:43,320
 financial situation now, God provided for us.

790
00:34:43,320 --> 00:34:48,320
 How many of you are, you're not allowing God

791
00:34:48,320 --> 00:34:51,000
 to come through in your life in powerful ways

792
00:34:51,000 --> 00:34:53,300
 because you're not obeying, why?

793
00:34:53,300 --> 00:34:57,160
 Because your hope is set on the uncertainty of riches.

794
00:34:57,160 --> 00:35:00,680
 God has called you to do something and step out of the boat

795
00:35:00,680 --> 00:35:03,380
 and you go, "I can't because the salary,

796
00:35:03,380 --> 00:35:05,100
 "I can't because how am I gonna live?

797
00:35:05,100 --> 00:35:08,360
 "I can't because," and so you won't obey.

798
00:35:08,360 --> 00:35:10,700
 You won't do that thing.

799
00:35:10,700 --> 00:35:12,740
 And maybe God is saying, not be lazy,

800
00:35:12,740 --> 00:35:15,360
 not just, oh, let go, let God, who cares?

801
00:35:15,360 --> 00:35:17,300
 No, you're gonna grind, you're gonna work hard,

802
00:35:17,300 --> 00:35:18,380
 but trust me.

803
00:35:18,380 --> 00:35:21,320
 I didn't know if I was gonna say this,

804
00:35:21,320 --> 00:35:23,020
 but I just think it's important.

805
00:35:23,020 --> 00:35:26,820
 When I got married, a mentor came to me and he said,

806
00:35:26,820 --> 00:35:29,380
 "Hey, husbands are supposed to do four things

807
00:35:29,380 --> 00:35:30,580
 "for their wives.

808
00:35:30,580 --> 00:35:34,020
 "They're supposed to protect, they're supposed to provide,

809
00:35:34,020 --> 00:35:35,780
 "they're supposed to pursue,

810
00:35:35,780 --> 00:35:39,220
 "and they're supposed to position them for success."

811
00:35:39,220 --> 00:35:42,640
 He said, "Tyler, when you and Jen get married,"

812
00:35:42,640 --> 00:35:44,120
 'cause he knew Jen wanted to work.

813
00:35:44,120 --> 00:35:45,320
 Jen was like, "I'm gonna work forever,

814
00:35:45,320 --> 00:35:46,420
 "this is gonna be great."

815
00:35:46,420 --> 00:35:48,760
 And we were setting up kind of our finances that way.

816
00:35:48,760 --> 00:35:52,460
 He said, "Hey, your job as a man is to be the provider.

817
00:35:52,460 --> 00:35:54,260
 "That doesn't mean your wife can't work.

818
00:35:54,260 --> 00:35:56,420
 "In fact, if she does work, praise God, that's awesome,

819
00:35:56,420 --> 00:35:57,520
 "live on two income.

820
00:35:57,520 --> 00:36:02,520
 "Just don't allow your living expenses,

821
00:36:02,520 --> 00:36:06,540
 "your lifestyle to supersede what you can afford,

822
00:36:06,540 --> 00:36:10,300
 "such that if any day she wants to stay home,

823
00:36:10,300 --> 00:36:13,920
 "feels convicted by God that she's supposed to stay home,

824
00:36:13,920 --> 00:36:15,780
 "that you would have to say back to her,

825
00:36:15,780 --> 00:36:19,000
 "we can't, 'cause I can't afford to pay for it."

826
00:36:19,000 --> 00:36:22,960
 And I know so many Christian guys

827
00:36:22,960 --> 00:36:25,040
 who their wives start to have that conviction

828
00:36:25,040 --> 00:36:27,440
 and they go, "Sorry, you gotta work,

829
00:36:27,440 --> 00:36:30,120
 "because we can't afford this lifestyle

830
00:36:30,120 --> 00:36:31,220
 "with just one income."

831
00:36:31,220 --> 00:36:35,060
 And I would go, "Well, figure it out, bro, figure it out.

832
00:36:35,060 --> 00:36:36,940
 "You gotta get a better job,

833
00:36:36,940 --> 00:36:41,140
 "or you gotta not get that new car, figure it out."

834
00:36:41,140 --> 00:36:43,300
 All right, we gotta keep moving.

835
00:36:43,300 --> 00:36:44,820
 Oh boy, we're a little behind.

836
00:36:44,820 --> 00:36:49,080
 Okay, verse 18, it says,

837
00:36:49,080 --> 00:36:53,000
 "They are to do good, to be rich in good works,

838
00:36:53,000 --> 00:36:55,060
 "to be generous and ready to share."

839
00:36:55,060 --> 00:36:58,600
 So the second thing that Paul says is,

840
00:36:58,600 --> 00:36:59,900
 man, to the rich people,

841
00:36:59,900 --> 00:37:01,640
 to the people who are wanting to be rich,

842
00:37:01,640 --> 00:37:04,580
 do good and be rich in good works.

843
00:37:04,580 --> 00:37:07,540
 Man, I have so many verses I wanna share and everything,

844
00:37:07,540 --> 00:37:09,120
 I'm just gonna get cut to the chase.

845
00:37:09,120 --> 00:37:10,640
 I think sometimes in Christian circles,

846
00:37:10,640 --> 00:37:12,120
 we do everything I just said.

847
00:37:12,120 --> 00:37:14,260
 We go, "Let go, let God, God's just gonna work it out."

848
00:37:14,260 --> 00:37:15,500
 So like, who cares about money?

849
00:37:15,500 --> 00:37:18,420
 The reality is, all through the New Testament,

850
00:37:18,420 --> 00:37:21,980
 all through Proverbs, it's look at the ant, man.

851
00:37:21,980 --> 00:37:24,820
 That guy's working, he's grinding.

852
00:37:24,820 --> 00:37:26,580
 God wants you to work.

853
00:37:26,580 --> 00:37:27,860
 It says in 2 Thessalonians,

854
00:37:27,860 --> 00:37:31,000
 "He who doesn't work, let him not eat."

855
00:37:31,000 --> 00:37:35,220
 Some of you, you're so good at asking people to support you.

856
00:37:35,220 --> 00:37:36,620
 You're support raised,

857
00:37:36,620 --> 00:37:39,060
 not because you're doing something,

858
00:37:39,060 --> 00:37:40,440
 like missions with your life,

859
00:37:40,440 --> 00:37:42,300
 just because you want people to take care of you.

860
00:37:42,300 --> 00:37:43,460
 You live at your parents' house,

861
00:37:43,460 --> 00:37:46,060
 not because it's the wise thing to do in this moment,

862
00:37:46,060 --> 00:37:47,600
 just 'cause you're lazy.

863
00:37:47,600 --> 00:37:50,280
 You live off of someone else's income,

864
00:37:50,280 --> 00:37:53,140
 not because it's what's wise in that season,

865
00:37:53,140 --> 00:37:54,260
 but because you're lazy.

866
00:37:54,260 --> 00:37:59,260
 And Paul's saying, "No, do good, be rich in good works.

867
00:37:59,260 --> 00:38:02,060
 "Figure out what you're good at and get paid for it.

868
00:38:02,060 --> 00:38:04,380
 "And don't be ashamed to go to your boss

869
00:38:04,380 --> 00:38:06,380
 "if you're working, grinding hard and going,

870
00:38:06,380 --> 00:38:08,720
 "Hey, I'm actually worth this."

871
00:38:08,720 --> 00:38:11,980
 Don't be a snot about it, but say it.

872
00:38:11,980 --> 00:38:14,340
 This is what I'm worth, I wanna be paid this.

873
00:38:14,340 --> 00:38:17,600
 That's okay, Christians, that's all right.

874
00:38:17,600 --> 00:38:19,820
 But don't go around mooching off of people

875
00:38:19,820 --> 00:38:20,820
 when you're not working.

876
00:38:20,820 --> 00:38:22,660
 Man, we could say so much more on that.

877
00:38:22,660 --> 00:38:24,220
 The second half of verse 18 says,

878
00:38:24,220 --> 00:38:27,300
 "Be generous and ready to share."

879
00:38:27,300 --> 00:38:29,940
 It doesn't just say, be generous,

880
00:38:29,940 --> 00:38:32,860
 and when someone asks for money, go ahead and do it.

881
00:38:32,860 --> 00:38:36,500
 It says, "Be ready, be eager to share."

882
00:38:36,500 --> 00:38:37,920
 Do you have this mentality

883
00:38:37,920 --> 00:38:40,500
 when it comes to giving in your life?

884
00:38:40,500 --> 00:38:43,060
 Remember a mentor of mine, he would in his wallet

885
00:38:43,060 --> 00:38:46,500
 carry two $20 bills that he called his giving fund.

886
00:38:46,500 --> 00:38:49,460
 He said, "Every month, I wanna give those $20 bills

887
00:38:49,460 --> 00:38:51,860
 "to someone and just bless 'em."

888
00:38:51,860 --> 00:38:54,940
 He called it his blessing fund, sorry, his blessing fund.

889
00:38:54,940 --> 00:38:57,200
 He said, "Whether it was someone at the gas station,

890
00:38:57,200 --> 00:38:58,440
 "as he's pumping gas, he's just like,

891
00:38:58,440 --> 00:39:00,500
 "You know what, I wanna pay for their gas.

892
00:39:00,500 --> 00:39:02,700
 "Whether it's a single mom that he sees,

893
00:39:02,700 --> 00:39:05,680
 "you know, paying at Costco and you just,

894
00:39:05,680 --> 00:39:07,140
 "20 bucks ain't gonna do much, but you know,

895
00:39:07,220 --> 00:39:11,780
 "just something or a really nice tip or whatever.

896
00:39:11,780 --> 00:39:12,620
 "I just wanna give."

897
00:39:12,620 --> 00:39:15,180
 Maybe in this day and age, inflation, it's 420s.

898
00:39:15,180 --> 00:39:17,500
 I don't know, but you're just prepared going,

899
00:39:17,500 --> 00:39:19,660
 "I wanna give, I wanna give."

900
00:39:19,660 --> 00:39:23,780
 I remember when I was a youth pastor,

901
00:39:23,780 --> 00:39:27,640
 I was driving to work and I got a flat

902
00:39:27,640 --> 00:39:28,620
 and I didn't have a spare,

903
00:39:28,620 --> 00:39:31,500
 so I'm like getting into the parking lot

904
00:39:31,500 --> 00:39:34,060
 and I had to figure out to get a tow truck and all this.

905
00:39:34,060 --> 00:39:35,420
 And my students, I didn't tell anybody,

906
00:39:35,420 --> 00:39:36,980
 my students heard about it.

907
00:39:36,980 --> 00:39:39,340
 And behind my back, they collected money.

908
00:39:39,340 --> 00:39:41,080
 And then when I went out to my car,

909
00:39:41,080 --> 00:39:42,560
 they put this on my car.

910
00:39:42,560 --> 00:39:43,920
 I think we have a picture of it.

911
00:39:43,920 --> 00:39:47,780
 It just said, "Tyler, for your tire,

912
00:39:47,780 --> 00:39:50,120
 "God loves you and sees you.

913
00:39:50,120 --> 00:39:53,380
 "Praying Philippians 1, 9 through 11, over you."

914
00:39:53,380 --> 00:39:54,860
 So my students put,

915
00:39:54,860 --> 00:39:57,020
 and I remember seeing that just being so excited.

916
00:39:57,020 --> 00:39:58,060
 And then I went and saw them,

917
00:39:58,060 --> 00:39:59,780
 they're all like hiding, like looking,

918
00:39:59,780 --> 00:40:01,460
 you know, waiting for me to see it.

919
00:40:01,460 --> 00:40:05,020
 And then they were just overjoyed.

920
00:40:05,020 --> 00:40:06,620
 I mean, students that didn't even like each other

921
00:40:06,620 --> 00:40:08,020
 were like, "Yeah, man, we did that."

922
00:40:08,020 --> 00:40:10,300
 You know, like they just were bonding.

923
00:40:10,300 --> 00:40:12,100
 Why? Because Jesus was right.

924
00:40:12,100 --> 00:40:15,020
 It's more blessed to give than to receive.

925
00:40:15,020 --> 00:40:18,220
 I've gone through times in my life

926
00:40:18,220 --> 00:40:21,340
 when I've just been in what I call a funk.

927
00:40:21,340 --> 00:40:23,940
 And I don't know if it's straight up depression

928
00:40:23,940 --> 00:40:24,940
 or if it's just whatever it is,

929
00:40:24,940 --> 00:40:26,220
 but there's just moments where I'm just like,

930
00:40:26,220 --> 00:40:27,600
 "Man, I am in a funk."

931
00:40:27,600 --> 00:40:31,060
 The only way I know how to get out of that

932
00:40:31,060 --> 00:40:34,180
 is by blessing someone else.

933
00:40:34,180 --> 00:40:37,620
 I gotta get in my car, go to Starbucks

934
00:40:37,620 --> 00:40:38,820
 and pay for the person behind me.

935
00:40:38,820 --> 00:40:40,060
 It's just like, oh man, I just,

936
00:40:40,060 --> 00:40:41,900
 something about it, I just feel better.

937
00:40:41,900 --> 00:40:42,940
 It's not for that purpose,

938
00:40:42,940 --> 00:40:47,460
 but just do you have in your life a rhythm of giving?

939
00:40:47,460 --> 00:40:50,460
 We're at church, so we gotta talk about this.

940
00:40:50,460 --> 00:40:52,600
 Tithing, okay?

941
00:40:52,600 --> 00:40:54,660
 If you're a Christian,

942
00:40:54,660 --> 00:40:55,920
 oh man, maybe that was the enemy.

943
00:40:55,920 --> 00:40:57,240
 My note just went away.

944
00:40:57,240 --> 00:41:00,220
 Oh boy, okay.

945
00:41:00,220 --> 00:41:01,740
 Tithing.

946
00:41:01,740 --> 00:41:03,380
 If you're a Christian,

947
00:41:03,380 --> 00:41:04,900
 there is nothing in the New Testament

948
00:41:04,900 --> 00:41:06,740
 that tells you to tithe.

949
00:41:06,740 --> 00:41:07,860
 I don't know if you know that.

950
00:41:07,860 --> 00:41:09,540
 There's not a verse in the New Testament that says,

951
00:41:09,540 --> 00:41:11,900
 "You better give 10% of your income to the church."

952
00:41:11,900 --> 00:41:13,300
 It doesn't exist.

953
00:41:13,300 --> 00:41:17,300
 The reality is what the New Testament says

954
00:41:17,300 --> 00:41:22,300
 is all of your life and all of your income is God's.

955
00:41:22,300 --> 00:41:24,220
 It's 100% His.

956
00:41:24,220 --> 00:41:29,100
 And now you're a steward of His resources in your life.

957
00:41:29,100 --> 00:41:30,640
 So what someone told me early on

958
00:41:30,640 --> 00:41:35,540
 is that the 10% is not the ceiling of what you should give.

959
00:41:35,540 --> 00:41:37,420
 It's the floor.

960
00:41:37,420 --> 00:41:39,340
 And what my wife and I've done throughout our marriage

961
00:41:39,340 --> 00:41:42,540
 is we've gone, regardless of if we like our church or not,

962
00:41:42,540 --> 00:41:45,820
 regardless of if we're on board with their leadership or not,

963
00:41:45,820 --> 00:41:49,460
 10% of our income is going to our church regardless.

964
00:41:49,460 --> 00:41:50,660
 And we want it to grow.

965
00:41:50,660 --> 00:41:52,940
 And through our marriage, it's grown.

966
00:41:52,940 --> 00:41:56,420
 And it was less about the church.

967
00:41:56,420 --> 00:42:00,820
 It was more about me getting my hands off of my money.

968
00:42:00,820 --> 00:42:03,160
 It was like God was saying,

969
00:42:03,160 --> 00:42:07,160
 "Tyler, I want you to trust me with 10%.

970
00:42:07,160 --> 00:42:08,300
 "Just give it."

971
00:42:08,300 --> 00:42:10,120
 Like recurring giving, just give it away.

972
00:42:10,120 --> 00:42:11,840
 'Cause I don't want you to see it.

973
00:42:11,840 --> 00:42:13,840
 I want you to learn to live on 90

974
00:42:13,840 --> 00:42:16,040
 and see 10 as an offering to me.

975
00:42:16,040 --> 00:42:18,040
 That doesn't mean you don't care what happens at the church.

976
00:42:18,040 --> 00:42:19,520
 Man, we should care.

977
00:42:19,520 --> 00:42:22,120
 But I'm saying, do you have that rhythm?

978
00:42:22,120 --> 00:42:24,280
 The reality is in a room like this,

979
00:42:24,280 --> 00:42:25,980
 you don't, many of you.

980
00:42:26,680 --> 00:42:28,840
 And maybe the application coming out of this sermon

981
00:42:28,840 --> 00:42:31,080
 is you start, whatever your local church is,

982
00:42:31,080 --> 00:42:32,560
 you start giving to them.

983
00:42:32,560 --> 00:42:34,860
 And young adults are the ones

984
00:42:34,860 --> 00:42:37,140
 not only fueling service in ministry,

985
00:42:37,140 --> 00:42:39,520
 but finances in ministry.

986
00:42:39,520 --> 00:42:44,780
 Last one, verse 19, it says,

987
00:42:44,780 --> 00:42:47,240
 "Thus storing up treasure for themselves

988
00:42:47,240 --> 00:42:49,240
 "as a good foundation for the future,

989
00:42:49,240 --> 00:42:53,220
 "so they may take hold of that which is truly life."

990
00:42:54,640 --> 00:42:58,060
 Paul says, "Man, to the rich, tell them,

991
00:42:58,060 --> 00:42:59,800
 "hey, open your eyes.

992
00:42:59,800 --> 00:43:02,280
 "Real life is offered to you.

993
00:43:02,280 --> 00:43:04,000
 "And it's not in the latest gadget

994
00:43:04,000 --> 00:43:07,620
 "or the latest monetary game."

995
00:43:07,620 --> 00:43:09,140
 That's not what it's in.

996
00:43:09,140 --> 00:43:11,700
 He says, "If you're living for temporary things,

997
00:43:11,700 --> 00:43:14,860
 "just for yourself, you're settling on real life."

998
00:43:14,860 --> 00:43:16,980
 Jesus in Matthew chapter 6, 33 will say,

999
00:43:16,980 --> 00:43:20,160
 "But seek first the kingdom of God and his righteousness,

1000
00:43:20,160 --> 00:43:23,060
 "and all these things will be added to you."

1001
00:43:24,040 --> 00:43:27,920
 I remember Francis Chan, a pastor in California,

1002
00:43:27,920 --> 00:43:32,320
 saying one time, "Live a life that demands an explanation."

1003
00:43:32,320 --> 00:43:37,320
 If you're living for yourself, if your finances,

1004
00:43:37,320 --> 00:43:39,880
 if you look at it, it's all about you,

1005
00:43:39,880 --> 00:43:43,560
 your sweet treat, your car, your housing situation,

1006
00:43:43,560 --> 00:43:45,680
 you, you, you, you, you,

1007
00:43:45,680 --> 00:43:47,760
 that doesn't demand an explanation.

1008
00:43:47,760 --> 00:43:49,800
 So you're obsessed with you, pretty easy.

1009
00:43:51,760 --> 00:43:55,460
 If someone were to look at your finances and your time,

1010
00:43:55,460 --> 00:43:59,000
 the way you spend your life, would they go, "What?

1011
00:43:59,000 --> 00:44:02,140
 "Wait, wait, hold on, what?

1012
00:44:02,140 --> 00:44:04,100
 "Why do you do that?"

1013
00:44:04,100 --> 00:44:07,280
 And would you just be able to point them to Jesus,

1014
00:44:07,280 --> 00:44:08,600
 what he's done in your life?

